/-!
# The lift-source audit — can the observer-level lift be formulated so that it supplies an
admissible intervention?

The preregistered pass of `LIFT-SOURCE-AUDIT.md`. The census of the corpus's formulations of the
lift is in the note; the kernel content is the tests of the formulations that land in the
operational interface, and the countermodel to the generator reading.

* T1, the diagonal criterion: a theory every one of whose available families preserves diagonal
  states executes no layer flow of an involution with a moved configuration
  (`not_layerFlowExecutable_of_preservesDiag`).
* T2, the coherent completion: the reversible coherent lift of a permutation with unimodular
  phases is monomial (`coherentLift_isMonomial`); the reversible coherent extension of a
  permutation is conjugation by a monomial isometry (`reversibleExtension_conj_monomial`); every
  member of the correlation family, reversible or not, preserves diagonal states
  (`correlationExtension_preservesDiag`); the class of the substratum's operators together with
  every reversible coherent lift of every permutation is configuration-level, is the substratum
  class, has the substratum's architecture and generates the substratum theory
  (`coherentLiftClass_contains_lift`, `coherentLiftClass_configurationLevel`,
  `coherentLiftClass_eq_substratumClass`, `coherentLiftClass_arch`,
  `coherentLiftTheory_eq_substratumTheory`), so it executes no layer flow of an involution with a
  moved configuration (`coherentLiftClass_not_layerFlowExecutable`); the observer theory of every
  substratum lies inside it (`obs_availExt_le_coherentLift`), and the wave substratum's
  lift-extended theory does not execute its own swap-layer flow
  (`waveSubstratum_coherentLift_not_layerFlowExecutable_swap`).
* T3, the projected observer operator: a scaled matrix unit is monomial (`single_isMonomial`);
  the explicit Kraus form of a classical stochastic map has monomial Kraus operators and the channel
  preserves diagonal states (`stochasticChannel_kraus_monomial`, `stochasticChannel_preservesDiag`); a theory
  generated by a class of monomials and scaled matrix units executes no layer flow of an
  involution with a moved configuration (`stochastic_not_layerFlowExecutable`).
* T4, the generator reading: the substratum theory has the gate of every involution available at
  time one at every level and executes its flow at no level when the involution moves a
  configuration (`avail_one_not_layerFlowExecutable`); the observer theory of every substratum
  has its swap layer available at time one and executes its flow at no level when the swap layer
  moves a configuration (`obs_swap_avail_one_not_layerFlowExecutable`).

Not claimed: that the wave-operator lift on the amplitude space is or is not derivable, or that a
map from it to the configuration carrier exists or does not; that every implementation of a
nonreversible coherent completion, or every Kraus realization of the stochastic channel, is
configuration-level, the reversible members being proved monomial and one monomial realization of
the channel exhibited; that any non-monomial admissible
operator yields the gate flow of a layer; anything about the phase; anything about a richer
observer architecture than the stated one; anything about a manuscript.
-/

